By the sum-to-product formula,
\[\sin 5 \theta - \sin \theta = 2 \sin 2 \theta \cos 3 \theta.\]Also,
\begin{align*}
\sin 5 \theta - \sin \theta &= \sin^5 \theta - \sin \theta \\
&= \sin \theta (\sin^4 \theta - 1) \\
&= \sin \theta (\sin^2 \theta + 1)(\sin^2 \theta - 1) \\
&= -\sin \theta (\sin^2 \theta + 1) \cos^2 \theta.
\end{align*}Hence,
\[2 \sin 2 \theta \cos 3 \theta = -\sin \theta (\sin^2 \theta + 1) \cos^2 \theta.\]Since $\theta$ is acute, $\sin \theta$ and $\cos \theta$ are nonzero.  Then
\[4 \sin \theta \cos \theta \cos 3 \theta = -(\sin^2 \theta + 1) \cos^2 \theta,\]so
\[4 \cos \theta \cos 3 \theta = -(\sin^2 \theta + 1) \cos \theta.\]Since $\cos \theta \neq 0,$ $4 \cos 3 \theta = -(\sin^2 \theta + 1).$  By the triple angle formula,
\[4 (4 \cos^3 \theta - 3 \cos \theta) = -(\sin^2 \theta + 1).\]Then $16 \cos^3 \theta - 12 \cos \theta = -\sin^2 \theta - 1,$ so
\[16 \cos^3 \theta - 11 \cos \theta + 1 = 0.\]This factors as $(\cos \theta - 1)(4 \cos \theta - 1)^2 = 0.$  Since $\theta$ is acute, $\cos \theta \neq 1,$ so $\cos \theta = \frac{1}{4}.$

